{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153637-conjunctional-subtle-arcana-what-am-i-missing-here","id":1153637,"title":"Conjunctional Subtle Arcana - What am I missing here?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-27T18:55:23-07:00","id":1153637,"title":"Conjunctional Subtle Arcana - What am I missing here?","content":"According to the Creative Thaumaturgy rules:<br /> <br /> &quot;A spell that transforms the target into something that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces), requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the destination Arcanum.&quot;<br /> <br /> But then we have spells like &quot;Shadow Flesh (Death 4)&quot; and &quot;Twilit Body (Spirit 4)&quot; that change your body to ephemera without adding Life to it.<br /> <br /> Do the Subtle Arcana bypass the above rule that it is required to know the destination Arcanum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:38:10-07:00","id":1153656,"title":"","content":"Death and Spirit both deal with physically manifesting ghosts and spirits (and goetia, even, in the context of conjunctional Arcana) and engaging in the state-change that enables one to move between the material world and the Underworld/the Shadow; Death and Spirit can convert a body to ephemera without Life even outside the auspices of Twilit Body just on the basis of how interdimensional travel works.<br /> <br /> The Subtle Arcana have broader purviews that can indirectly mess with things under the Gross Arcana, but inter-Arcana Patterning is mostly relevant when you're crossing unambiguously from one field to another, like by bringing different ephemeral beings into phase with one another or effecting the aforesaid pillar-of-fire state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:42:28-07:00","id":1153658,"title":"","content":"Shadow Flesh doesn't turn you into ephemera. Death and Spirit already render transformative processes on the living though, for instance when you cross into Twilight or the Shadow or Underworld you're turned into ephemera. Shadow Flesh is a tweak of that to change you from an ephemeral being via entering Twilight into a different kind of being, one of shadows which also falls under Death's purview. Twilit Body on the other hand is just a way to enter the Spirit attuned phase of Twilight by being made of spirit ephemera which is already something people passing into the Shadow become.<br /> <br /> So, it's not that the subtle arcana bypass the rule, so much as that they have some creative applications that aren't necessarily apparent on the surface of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T03:11:45-07:00","id":1153700,"title":"","content":"Also death gets to cheat a bit because transforming something from being governed by the life arcarnum to governed by the death arcarnum is something <i>every</i> arcarnum can do. Because you can kill people with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T15:27:23-07:00","id":1153815,"title":"","content":"The way I read it, destination Arcanum is the Arcanum that governes the end point of transformation. So:<br /> <br /> &quot;Flesh -&gt; Shadows&quot; would use Death,<br /> &quot;Flesh -&gt; Ephemera&quot; -- Spirit,<br /> &quot;Flesh -&gt; Stone&quot; -- Matter,<br /> <br /> It leads to strange things like:<br /> &quot;Stone -&gt; Memory&quot; -- Mind<br /> <br /> So I houserule that you need both Arcanums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T21:37:16-07:00","id":1153873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"120\" data-vbnamecard=\"120\">Daimon</a> That's not a houserule, unless you're ignoring certain aspects of the arcana. A memory/stone hybrid would need Mind+Matter, for instance, but when a person steps through a Verge into Shadow they become ephemera, so it's part of the Spirit arcana to render flesh into ephemera with a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}